{
  "schema": "holoscript.frame-allowlist-cases.v2",
  "about": "G15 (proposals/Agent_Frame_Tool_Allowlist_v1.md). Each case is one @frame_declaration and what every reader that reads it must produce. The readers: the canonical .hsplus parser (packages/core, HoloScriptPlusParser), the Rust grammar authority (packages/compiler-wasm ast.rs and parser.rs), and the agent loader (packages/holoscript-agent brain.ts), whose frame is what an agent sends to the MCP gate. A case is built from its body with one of the wraps below; core and the agent place the result inside a brain, Rust reads it at the top level. \"allowed_tools\" is what the canonical parser reads (when it refuses the case: what the readers that do read it produce). A reader that reads a case differently has its own entry: \"core\", \"rust\" or \"agent\" holds \"rejects\" (that reader refuses the source; the agent loader throws) or the list that reader produces instead. The agent's list may only ever be narrower than the canonical one: it never permits a tool the canonical frame denies. \"rust_frames\" lists the frame nodes the Rust reader returns when a case declares more than one; it combines none of them. \"permits\" and \"denies\" name tools the case's allowed_tools must permit or deny when enforced (core's checkToolAllowed, and the MCP gate); they appear only on cases every reader reads alike.",
  "wrap": {
    "braces": "@frame_declaration {\n<body>\n}",
    "parens": "@frame_declaration(<body>)",
    "source": "<body>"
  },
  "cases": [
    {
