    {
      "id": "apostrophe-in-code-before-header",
      "form": "source",
      "body": "note: it's locked @frame_declaration {\nallowed_tools: [\"read\"]\n}",
      "allowed_tools": [
        "read"
      ],
      "core": "rejects",
      "rust": "rejects",
      "note": "A quote that does not close on its line cannot hide a frame from the agent: it is read as code. Core and Rust refuse the unclosed string."
    },
    {
      "id": "line-comment-between-name-and-brace",
      "form": "source",
      "body": "@frame_declaration // c\n{\nallowed_tools: [\"read\"]\n}",
      "allowed_tools": [
        "read"
      ],
      "core": "rejects",
      "note": "Core takes a header at the end of its line as a frame with no block, and the block on the next line then fails to parse, so core refuses the source. Rust and the agent skip the comment and the line break and read the block."
    },
    {
      "id": "line-break-between-name-and-brace",
      "form": "source",
      "body": "@frame_declaration\n{\nallowed_tools: [\"read\"]\n}",
      "allowed_tools": [
        "read"
      ],
      "core": "rejects",
      "note": "As with the line comment: core refuses the source; Rust and the agent read the block on the next line."
    },
    {
      "id": "header-then-unreadable-text",
      "form": "source",
      "body": "@frame_declaration = {\nallowed_tools: [\"read\"]\n}",
      "allowed_tools": [],
      "core": "rejects",
      "rust": "rejects",
      "note": "A header followed by something that is not a block: core and Rust refuse the source, the agent sends no tool."
    },
    {
      "id": "header-then-comment-that-never-closes",
      "form": "source",
      "body": "@frame_declaration /* never closed {\nallowed_tools: [\"read\"]\n}",
      "allowed_tools": [],
      "core": "rejects",
      "rust": [
        "*"
      ],
      "note": "Both lexers read a block comment that never closes to the end of the file. Inside a brain that swallows the brain's closing brace, so core refuses; Rust, at the top level, is left with a bare header and reads every tool. Rust enforces no frame. The agent cannot find a block after the header, so it sends no tool."
    },
    {
      "id": "bare-header",
      "form": "source",
      "body": "@frame_declaration",
      "allowed_tools": [
        "*"
      ],
      "agent": [],
      "note": "Core and Rust read a header with no block as a frame with every default, so every tool. The agent cannot tell what the author meant to follow the header, so it sends no tool."
    },
